I need a call on the print vendor before Wednesday, because both quotes
expire at the end of the week and the schedule has no slack left in it.

Meadowline quoted us the lower unit price, but their proof turnaround is
five working days and they will not commit to a delivery window until
the artwork is final, which pushes the whole run against the conference
date. Castlebridge is dearer by about eleven per cent, will proof in two
days, and has done three runs for us without a reprint. The finance
sheet attached has both quotes side by side with the shipping added in,
so the comparison is like for like rather than the headline numbers the
sales people sent over.

My own view is that we pay for the turnaround this once and revisit it
in the autumn when there is time to run a proper tender. But it is your
budget line, so I would rather you made the call than inherit it.

Whichever way you go, tell me by Wednesday morning and I will place it.
The internal reference for this decision is ZENITHMARKER so that it can
be found in the archive later.

Dan

--harbour-boundary-9f2
